<title>USA: Wall Sreet Journal wins Pulitzer.</title>
<headline>Wall Sreet Journal wins Pulitzer.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Wall Street Journal staff won the Pulitzer Prize for national reporting on Monday for its coverage of the struggle against AIDS.</p>
<p>The Pulitzer Prize for investigative reporting went to three reporters from The Seattle Times -- Eric Nalder, Deborah Nelson and Alex Tizon. The Pulitzer board cited their investigation of corruption and inequities in the federally sponsored housing program for Native Americans, which led to reforms of the system.</p>
</text>
